[2026-03-29 01:01:02] Expanded SCB report routing to per-fault handlers, fixed SCB asm report arguments, and added UART SCB reporters with startup registration.
- Request: Correct the large SCB report change by making SCB_Report store handlers per SCB_nFAULT entry, pass SCB_nFAULT explicitly into register/unregister/invoke, ensure every GNU/TI SCB report-stage asm call sets R0 and R1 before calling __vIRQVectorHandlerReport, add UART handlers for each SCB fault family, and register them in startup.
- API refactor: Updated xApplication_MCU/Core/SCB/xHeader/SCB_Report.h and xSource/SCB_Report.c so report handlers are stored in a per-fault array with independent context pointers, and changed SCB__enRegisterReportHandler(...), SCB__enUnregisterReportHandler(...), and SCB__vInvokeReportHandler(...) to take SCB_nFAULT explicitly.
- SCB integration: Modified BusFault, MemoryFault, UsageFault, HardFault, and NMI report-stage code to invoke the per-fault report slot using stReport.enFault instead of the previous global handler path.
- Assembly fix: Updated GNU and TI SCB vector stubs for BusFault, MemoryFault, UsageFault, and HardFault so they load SCB_BASE into R0 and the corresponding saved context buffer into R1 before calling the report-stage handler, then reload the same arguments before calling the custom-stage handler.
- UART integration: Added xApplication_MCU/UART/xHeader/UART_SCB.h and xSource/UART_SCB.c with separate UART callbacks for usage fault, bus fault, memory fault, hard fault, and NMI, each using its own source-message table while sharing a common formatted register-dump printer.
- Startup integration: Updated TM4C129E_Project/tm4c129encpdt_startup_ccs.c to include UART_SCB.h and register all five SCB report callbacks on UART7 before the existing SYSEXC report registration.
- Validation: VS Code diagnostics report no errors in TM4C129E_DriverLib/xApplication_MCU/Core/SCB and TM4C129E_DriverLib/xApplication_MCU/UART after these changes. The startup file still shows the same pre-existing parser errors around main() and the trailing brace; no new startup-specific diagnostics attributable to the SCB/UART edits were reported.